P4. Emitted assembly, aarch64-apple-darwin, rustc 1.98.0-nightly (57d06900f), -O
=============================================================================

Local label numbering normalised (LBB<n>_<k> -> LBB_<k>); nothing else touched.

  direct_wrap        9 instructions
  pref_speed         9 instructions
  direct_widen      39 instructions
  pref_accuracy     39 instructions

  direct_wrap   == pref_speed     : True
  direct_widen  == pref_accuracy  : False
  direct_wrap   == direct_widen   : False   <- must be False or the comparison above is vacuous

  direct_wrap / pref_speed body:
      mov x8, #0
      cbz x1, LBB_2
      ldr w9, [x0], #8
      add w8, w9, w8
      and x8, x8, #0xfff
      subs x1, x1, #1
      b.ne LBB_1
      mov x0, x8
      ret


Addendum: the widen pair is NOT instruction-identical. Located, not reported.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  instruction count      : 39 vs 39
  differing lines        : 4 of 39
  opcode MULTISET equal   : True
  opcode SEQUENCE equal   : False

  The four differing instructions, side by side:
      --- direct_widen
      +++ pref_accuracy
      @@ -29,11 +29,11 @@
      -sub x10, x1, x9
      -add x9, x0, x9, lsl #3
      -ldr x11, [x9], #8
      +add x10, x0, x9, lsl #3
      +sub x9, x1, x9
      +ldr x11, [x10], #8
      -subs x10, x10, #1
      +subs x9, x9, #1

  Reading. The opcode multiset is identical and the sequence is not: two
  adjacent, mutually independent instructions (an `add` computing an
  address and a `sub` computing a trip count) are scheduled in the
  opposite order, and the register allocator then assigns x9 and x10 the
  other way round. No instruction is added, none is removed, and there is
  no branch on anything the cost model produced.

  So the honest claim is narrower than 'identical output': the cost model
  leaves NO residue, evidenced by an identical opcode multiset and count,
  while the backend's scheduling is not stable across two call sites of
  the same inlined body. The wrap pair happens to be identical line for
  line; the widen pair is not, and that difference is the scheduler's.
